        "custom_liquid_aRertz": {
          "type": "custom_liquid",
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "<style>\n  .nu-faq {\n    max-width: 800px;\n    width: 100%;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 16px;\n    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-item {\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-item:first-child {\n    border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-question {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    gap: 12px;\n    padding: 20px 4px;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    font-size: clamp(17px, 2.5vw, 21px);\n    color: #1a1a1a;\n  }\n  .nu-plus {\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n    width: 16px;\n    height: 16px;\n    position: relative;\n    color: #3E4E3E;\n  }\n  .nu-plus::before,\n  .nu-plus::after {\n    content: '';\n    position: absolute;\n    background: currentColor;\n    transition: transform 0.25s ease;\n  }\n  .nu-plus::before {\n    top: 0; left: 50%;\n    width: 2px; height: 100%;\n    transform: translateX(-50%);\n  }\n  .nu-plus::after {\n    top: 50%; left: 0;\n    width: 100%; height: 2px;\n    transform: translateY(-50%);\n  }\n  .nu-faq-item.active .nu-plus::before {\n    transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(90deg);\n    opacity: 0;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-answer {\n    max-height: 0;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    transition: max-height 0.35s ease;\n    padding: 0 4px;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-item.active .nu-faq-answer {\n    max-height: 600px;\n    padding-bottom: 20px;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-answer p {\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n    font-size: clamp(13.5px, 1.9vw, 15px);\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    color: #444;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-answer p:last-child {\n    margin-bottom: 0;\n  }\n  .nu-faq-answer ol,\n  .nu-faq-answer ul {\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n    padding-left: 20px;\n    font-size: clamp(13.5px, 1.9vw, 15px);\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    color: #444;\n  }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"nu-faq\">\n\n  <div class=\"nu-faq-item\">\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-question\">\n      <span>Ingredients</span>\n      <span class=\"nu-plus\"></span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-answer\">\n      <p>Aqua/Water/Eau, Butylene Glycol, Glycerin, Dimethyl Isosorbide, Phenoxyethanol, Polyacrylate Crosspolymer-6, Hydroxyethyl Acrylate/Sodium Acryloyldimethyl Taurate Copolymer, Larrea Divaricata Leaf Extract, Bakuchiol, PEG-40 Hydrogenated Castor Oil, Trideceth-9, Fragrance (Parfum), Vaccinium Myrtillus Fruit Extract, Propanediol, Sugarcane Extract, Ascorbyl Tetraisopalmitate, Ethylhexylglycerin, Lecithin, Sorbitan Isostearate, Propylene Glycol, Orange Fruit Extract, Lemon Fruit Extract, Methylglucoside Phosphate, Ascorbic Acid, Carnosine, and other supporting botanical extracts and preservatives.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"nu-faq-item\">\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-question\">\n      <span>How does it actually work?</span>\n      <span class=\"nu-plus\"></span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-answer\">\n      <p>Glide works beneath the surface by blocking ATP (the \"energy molecule\") from reaching your hair follicles. Think of ATP as the fuel your follicles need to produce hair — when follicles receive this energy, they grow hair nonstop, which is why you're stuck in the endless cycle of removal.</p>\n      <p>Glide interrupts this process at the source. With less energy reaching the follicles:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Your hair takes twice as long to grow back</li>\n        <li>The texture becomes softer and finer</li>\n        <li>Regrowth is barely visible instead of coarse stubble</li>\n        <li>You can go weeks longer between removal sessions</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Unlike shaving, waxing, or plucking, which only remove hair temporarily, Glide changes how it grows back from the root.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"nu-faq-item\">\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-question\">\n      <span>Shipping and Returns</span>\n      <span class=\"nu-plus\"></span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-answer\">\n      <p>All NU:YU orders get free shipping straight from our USA warehouse. Orders are usually shipped within 1-2 working days, arriving within 3-7 working days for domestic USA orders, and within 10 working days for international orders.</p>\n      <p>We also offer a 60-day money-back guarantee — if you're unsatisfied with Glide Serum, you can ship the product back to us for a full refund within 60 days of receiving your order.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"nu-faq-item\">\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-question\">\n      <span>Instructions</span>\n      <span class=\"nu-plus\"></span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"nu-faq-answer\">\n      <p><b>How to Use Glide:</b></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Remove hair from the root by waxing, plucking, or epilating as normal</li>\n        <li>Wait 8-12 hours after hair removal</li>\n        <li>Massage a thin layer of Glide onto freshly cleansed skin</li>\n        <li>Repeat twice daily for best results</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>The lightweight serum absorbs quickly and won't interfere with your makeup or skincare routine.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function() {\n  document.querySelectorAll('.nu-faq-question').forEach(q => {\n    q.addEventListener('click', function() {\n      const item = this.parentElement;\n      const wasActive = item.classList.contains('active');\n      document.querySelectorAll('.nu-faq-item').forEach(i => i.classList.remove('active'));\n      if (!wasActive) item.classList.add('active');\n    });\n  });\n})();\n</script>"
          }
        }
